A||N||2||87 Sport Coupe||Friend redid my spark plugs to 30 not 60 on my 2.5 is that bad????||||4||
Z||000000||87 Sport Coupe||06-25-2001||02:06 AM||||Ok here it goes (Oh yeah this Forum is Awesome)Ok one of my friends came over when I was replacing the plugs in my 2.5 Gutless wonder...He said that I should put them on 30 unstood of the factory 60....so he did this and we put them in...The car idle was off for a while but then she pulled out and seems ok now....He said it would give her a lil more zip...I dont notice this more zip,he talked about besides the fact that it revs up to 5k a lot better now it does it as easy as it used to rev up to 3k....Ok so I have been told by another friend that because he did this I might burn my valves up? or worse.... so please let me know of all the bad things if there is any big ones.... Ok next thing my car has like 100k miles on it and my Fan runs non stop... Replace all the dang sensors I could find that it might be and then I even unplugged the lead into the ac comp. and still runs...any ideals(it isnt wired across just started doing this out of no-where.....The next thing is I start to drive my car and it wont hardly run untill its warmed up for a few mints and if you try to drive it..well you have to rev it really high or it will stall out(5 speed) Then once it warms up seems ok so your going along and its fine then after about sometimes 4 miles sometimes 15 miles when you let off the gas the service Motor soon light kicks on.... But only after you have drove a little bit and you let off the gas....I have checked for codes the only one I am getting is the dang V.S.S which the book said pay it no mind if the car isnt being drove.... I had the two prob. I just talked about before the new Ac Delco plugs was put in so thats not it... My o2 was just replaced,my Cat is there but well it isnt if you know what that means.... I have replaced the Tps... The car get decent mileage between 30-35 if I dont run it really hard... The idle on it goes up and down when its not being drove... Goes from between 900-1500...sometimes when coming to a red light if I go into netural it will drop to 400 then bounce back up and down till I tap the gas.... When it has set and had time to cool off when first started it goes up to 2000 rpms for a few then slowly goes down.... I have been told maybe my Iac...But I have no Code for this.... so any help on this is Wonderful....<BR>Thanks Guys your the best...<BR>DonnieH||||reg||4
Z||000001||SteveJ||06-25-2001||08:48 AM||||Paragraphs my friend were invented for a reason.<P>No you are not causing any damage with the smaller spark gap. You may have lost some small percentage of efficiency, however. DIS engines are designed for the larger gap and depend on the longer gap to ignite the more accuratly delivered fuel mixture. <P>You say the car runs better. It's probably due to the new plugs not the smaller gap.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||06-25-2001||08:37 PM||||Well... first off, unless you ignition has some other problem, you aren't helping a thing with a small gap. If I was going to do a smaller gap, I certainly wouldn't cut it by half. 45-50 at the absolute smallest. Keep in mind, DIS makes over Twice the power of HEI. (And no... I would not change the gap. I run mine at 060) Just putting in new plugs is prbably what made most of your diferance.<P>Fan running is a short in the control line or the realy is bad.<P>Clear the codes. then check them. VSS should Not set in these ECM's unless there is a real VSS problem.<P>Flakey idle, check the charging system, battery cables, all that. Screwy alt can cause wierd idle.<P>Check all the vac lines and the base of the TBI for leaks. check for loose EGR.<P>Next thing to check is MAP and it's vac line. The next is MAT to the right of the TBI. If MAT is cooked then it won't give the ECM correct data.<P><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 06-25-2001).]||||reg||1
